787
00:29:36,936 --> 00:29:40,686
- Our lady of from which
there is no escape.

788
00:29:41,868 --> 00:29:43,682
(speaks foreign language)

789
00:29:43,682 --> 00:29:44,515
- Will you get out of my way

790
00:29:44,515 --> 00:29:46,645
or do I have to beat you out of here?

791
00:29:46,645 --> 00:29:48,947
- Yeah, Beverly, go get her.

792
00:29:48,947 --> 00:29:49,780
- Ah, leave her alone.

793
00:29:49,780 --> 00:29:50,750
- Stay out of this.

794
00:29:50,750 --> 00:29:51,920
- Leave her alone!

795
00:29:51,920 --> 00:29:53,640
- She got in my way.

796
00:29:53,640 --> 00:29:55,720
- Wanna knock somebody
around, try your own size!

797
00:29:55,720 --> 00:29:57,246
- Like who?

798
00:29:57,246 --> 00:29:58,086
- Me.

799
00:29:58,086 --> 00:29:59,953
- Hey that does make a lot more sense.

800
00:29:59,953 --> 00:30:01,256
- Why don't you shut up.

801
00:30:01,256 --> 00:30:04,603
- It's Lucy and Viv, in the big house.

802
00:30:04,603 --> 00:30:07,020
- Welcome to dye job theater.

803
00:30:08,147 --> 00:30:10,543
- Well if you two ain't
a sight for sore eyes.

804
00:30:10,543 --> 00:30:11,940
- They're all doing a nickel at UPS.

805
00:30:11,940 --> 00:30:13,039
- I don't know about your eyes,

806
00:30:13,039 --> 00:30:14,772
but I sure have a sore back.

807
00:30:14,772 --> 00:30:15,638
- Not from working.

808
00:30:15,638 --> 00:30:16,471
- Whoa.

809
00:30:18,367 --> 00:30:20,332
- I just thought I'd drop around.

810
00:30:20,332 --> 00:30:23,097
- You'll get yourself put in
the brick for being down here.

811
00:30:23,097 --> 00:30:24,930
- There may be trustee

812
00:30:25,792 --> 00:30:26,786
- Typical.

813
00:30:26,786 --> 00:30:27,619
- We got no room.

814
00:30:27,619 --> 00:30:28,872
- Miss Leona.

815
00:30:28,872 --> 00:30:30,994
- They sure like to make
trouble for us, don't they?

816
00:30:30,994 --> 00:30:32,414
- She's crazier than a bed bug.

817
00:30:32,414 --> 00:30:33,698
- How can you tell?

818
00:30:33,698 --> 00:30:35,356
- She's only been here three hours,

819
00:30:35,356 --> 00:30:37,781
she wants to go over the wall.

820
00:30:37,781 --> 00:30:39,734
- Don't sound so crazy to me.

821
00:30:39,734 --> 00:30:41,060
- We let her climb over the wall,

822
00:30:41,060 --> 00:30:42,459
they shoot her and we're rid of her.

823
00:30:42,459 --> 00:30:44,376
- Yes, Mrs. Zelda Jane.

824
00:30:48,277 --> 00:30:50,852
- Guys, it's a prison slumber party.

825
00:30:50,852 --> 00:30:51,795
- They use razors in the pillows,

826
00:30:51,795 --> 00:30:53,628
for the pillow fights.

827
00:30:54,790 --> 00:30:56,987
- Okay, I'm a cop, don't hurt me.

828
00:30:56,987 --> 00:30:59,268
- When moms go bad.

829
00:30:59,268 --> 00:31:00,210
- Move it.

830
00:31:00,210 --> 00:31:01,598
- Shut up!

831
00:31:01,598 --> 00:31:03,131
- Oh, both of you shut up.

832
00:31:03,131 --> 00:31:04,708
- They're all strung out on Correctol.

833
00:31:04,708 --> 00:31:07,028
- Don't you know we're
very hard to get along.

834
00:31:07,028 --> 00:31:09,899
- Well I wasn't thinking
of a pleasure trip.

835
00:31:09,899 --> 00:31:13,075
- Well, what were you
thinking of, suicide?

836
00:31:13,075 --> 00:31:15,220
- No, the Nardo diamonds.

837
00:31:15,220 --> 00:31:17,665
- Wouldn't you just want
to get your hands on them.

838
00:31:17,665 --> 00:31:19,033
- Wouldn't you?

839
00:31:19,033 --> 00:31:21,126
- Look, we've been in here
for three lousy years.

840
00:31:21,126 --> 00:31:22,224
- What makes you think right away

841
00:31:22,224 --> 00:31:24,235
you can crash this joint?

842
00:31:24,235 --> 00:31:26,152
- Well I did something
you three girls didn't.

843
00:31:26,152 --> 00:31:28,037
- She was delouced.

844
00:31:28,037 --> 00:31:30,058
- Man, I didn't think we'd miss nothing.

845
00:31:30,058 --> 00:31:31,332
- Such as what?

846
00:31:31,332 --> 00:31:34,386
- On my way in, I planned a way out.

847
00:31:34,386 --> 00:31:35,435
- Just like that?

848
00:31:35,435 --> 00:31:36,268
- Oh, we should have done that.

849
00:31:36,268 --> 00:31:37,101
- Yes.

850
00:31:37,101 --> 00:31:38,035
(bell ringing)

851
00:31:38,035 --> 00:31:40,202
- Which twin has the tony.

852
00:31:41,044 --> 00:31:43,665
- Cool it the RA is coming.

853
00:31:43,665 --> 00:31:47,241
- A prison filled with Wendy Darlings.

854
00:31:47,241 --> 00:31:48,910
- Bring me that case of tea.

855
00:31:48,910 --> 00:31:52,069
- And they are ahead of Alfredo Garcia.

856
00:31:52,069 --> 00:31:54,569
- The true story of lands end.

857
00:31:55,966 --> 00:31:58,225
- What makes you so sure
we will split with you?

858
00:31:58,225 --> 00:32:00,204
- What makes you sure that
I'll take you with me?

859
00:32:00,204 --> 00:32:01,527
- Anyway, be quiet about our secret plan!

860
00:32:01,527 --> 00:32:03,704
- It'll be there.

861
00:32:03,704 --> 00:32:05,063
- Who's putting it there?

862
00:32:05,063 --> 00:32:06,326
- None of your business.

863
00:32:06,326 --> 00:32:07,247
- But who else will be there?

864
00:32:07,247 --> 00:32:10,330
Can I bring Susan, from cell block A?

865
00:32:11,475 --> 00:32:13,713
- Boy, she sure thinks she's hot.

866
00:32:13,713 --> 00:32:16,429
- I think she is too, if
she can get us out of here.

867
00:32:16,429 --> 00:32:19,093
- Sale's have gone up
since she's been here.

868
00:32:19,093 --> 00:32:22,481
- Back now, vinyl window theater.

869
00:32:22,481 --> 00:32:25,921
- See, they come apart,
but keep it a secret.

870
00:32:25,921 --> 00:32:27,735
- We've been doing a little planning too.

871
00:32:27,735 --> 00:32:29,423
- It's a long drop.

872
00:32:29,423 --> 00:32:30,256
- What's the matter?

873
00:32:30,256 --> 00:32:31,089
No guts?

874
00:32:31,089 --> 00:32:32,004
- Takes more than guts.

875
00:32:32,004 --> 00:32:34,171
- Still it does take guts.

876
00:32:35,661 --> 00:32:37,443
- How much are the diamonds worth?

877
00:32:37,443 --> 00:32:40,200
- Will give us 200 grand.

878
00:32:40,200 --> 00:32:41,743
- Can you find them?

879
00:32:41,743 --> 00:32:43,194
- I can find them.

880
00:32:43,194 --> 00:32:45,402
- I get 50 grand.

881
00:32:45,402 --> 00:32:47,247
- Yeah, 50 grand.

882
00:32:47,247 --> 00:32:48,251
- So if you ever have to leave,

883
00:32:48,251 --> 00:32:50,106
that's how to do it.

884
00:32:50,106 --> 00:32:51,189
- Stand back.

885
00:32:52,579 --> 00:32:54,579
- It's morning in Juliet

886
00:32:57,107 --> 00:32:58,330
- I can hardly sleep, how about you?

887
00:32:58,330 --> 00:32:59,979
I'm so excited!

888
00:32:59,979 --> 00:33:02,538
- We're going to be the first ones in line

889
00:33:02,538 --> 00:33:04,121
for scrambled eggs!

890
00:33:06,195 --> 00:33:08,241
- Wait a minute, it worked yesterday,

891
00:33:08,241 --> 00:33:09,411
I don't know what happened.

892
00:33:09,411 --> 00:33:12,828
- Well, it was loose so I welded it back.

893
00:33:13,670 --> 00:33:15,465
- These women are actually escaping

894
00:33:15,465 --> 00:33:18,046
in easy spirit dress pumps.

895
00:33:18,046 --> 00:33:21,434
- No one has ever escaped
from cell block 15.

896
00:33:21,434 --> 00:33:23,549
- Of course not.

897
00:33:23,549 --> 00:33:25,103
- Tell me boy, what day is this?

898
00:33:25,103 --> 00:33:26,832
- It's Christmas day, sir.

899
00:33:26,832 --> 00:33:27,983
- Oh, praise your name.

900
00:33:27,983 --> 00:33:30,816
- What's with the Get Smart music?

901
00:33:32,687 --> 00:33:34,148
- Okay, let's go!

902
00:33:34,148 --> 00:33:34,981
Ah!

903
00:33:39,744 --> 00:33:40,577
- Ah!

904
00:33:42,272 --> 00:33:45,439
- Don't forget to bring me a Dove bar.

905
00:33:47,144 --> 00:33:48,727
- This is riveting.

906
00:33:50,200 --> 00:33:51,200
- Cast away!

907
00:33:55,828 --> 00:33:56,661
- Wait, we can't leave.

908
00:33:56,661 --> 00:33:59,494
They're having creamed corn today!

909
00:34:01,827 --> 00:34:03,474
- Why am I thinking of Joe Theisman?

910
00:34:03,474 --> 00:34:06,057
(bell ringing)

911
00:34:08,127 --> 00:34:09,950
- I hit the bell on my way out.

912
00:34:09,950 --> 00:34:11,536
I hope that's okay.

913
00:34:11,536 --> 00:34:13,196
(alarm blaring)

914
00:34:13,196 --> 00:34:16,863
(speaking foreign language)

915
00:34:17,941 --> 00:34:18,774
(gunshots)

916
00:34:18,774 --> 00:34:21,112
- Sounds like the Foley
artists are chasing us,

917
00:34:21,112 --> 00:34:22,771
let's hit it!

918
00:34:22,771 --> 00:34:26,271
- The kids in the hall escape from prison!

919
00:34:28,499 --> 00:34:31,999
(speaks foreign language)

920
00:34:36,158 --> 00:34:37,256
- That's it.

921
00:34:37,256 --> 00:34:38,283
- Hey, let's take this one.

922
00:34:38,283 --> 00:34:40,489
This one is nice!

923
00:34:40,489 --> 00:34:43,204
- Budget rent a car is so convenient.

924
00:34:43,204 --> 00:34:45,350
- Oh, it's so roomy, such a nice car.

925
00:34:45,350 --> 00:34:47,049
- Oh, and look it's so clean.

926
00:34:47,049 --> 00:34:48,365
- With the floor mats and everything.

927
00:34:48,365 --> 00:34:50,085
- That new car smell.

928
00:34:50,085 --> 00:34:52,872
- Oh, the Wells Fargo wagon.

929
00:34:52,872 --> 00:34:53,705
- Look out.

930
00:34:53,705 --> 00:34:54,800
(gunshots)

931
00:34:54,800 --> 00:34:56,716
Boy, I sure do wish I had a gun.

932
00:34:56,716 --> 00:34:58,189
- Ouch, take it easy.

933
00:34:58,189 --> 00:34:59,060
- What's the matter?

934
00:34:59,060 --> 00:35:01,477
- I hurt my arm, that's what.

935
00:35:03,697 --> 00:35:04,614
- That one?

936
00:35:06,267 --> 00:35:08,335
- Ladies, it's a big car,
you can spread out a little.

937
00:35:08,335 --> 00:35:09,168
- Where do we go from here?

938
00:35:09,168 --> 00:35:10,001
- We're losing him.

939
00:35:10,001 --> 00:35:11,041
- Turn left half mile up.

940
00:35:11,041 --> 00:35:12,356
- I'm up for something chickeny.

941
00:35:12,356 --> 00:35:13,523
- Louie Blank?

942
00:35:14,398 --> 00:35:15,496
- Yeah.

943
00:35:15,496 --> 00:35:17,133
- Hey you think they'll give
us something decent to wear,

944
00:35:17,133 --> 00:35:18,697
and some lipstick.

945
00:35:18,697 --> 00:35:20,304
- Good enough for where we are going.

946
00:35:20,304 --> 00:35:21,423
- They've given up.

947
00:35:21,423 --> 00:35:22,977
- Boy, how do I wish I could have taken

948
00:35:22,977 --> 00:35:24,251
a couple of shots at them.

949
00:35:24,251 --> 00:35:26,976
(speaks fast imitating red haired woman)

950
00:35:26,976 --> 00:35:28,625
- You will if he knows
what's good for him.

951
00:35:28,625 --> 00:35:30,621
- How long do you think
it's gonna take us, Josie?

952
00:35:30,621 --> 00:35:32,756
- Well, it's a couple
of days with the boys.

953
00:35:32,756 --> 00:35:34,641
I don't see how we can do much better.

954
00:35:34,641 --> 00:35:35,562
- On foot?

955
00:35:35,562 --> 00:35:36,444
- In these shoes?

956
00:35:36,444 --> 00:35:38,881
- On foot it'd take
about a couple of years.

957
00:35:38,881 --> 00:35:41,377
- Louie'll give us a boat.

958
00:35:41,377 --> 00:35:43,115
We got a few things on Louie.

959
00:35:43,115 --> 00:35:45,900
- Yeah, we saw him coming
out of lend me a tenner.

960
00:35:45,900 --> 00:35:48,410
(car screeches)

961
00:35:48,410 --> 00:35:51,569
- I'm spritzing, any of you
mugs got a problem with that?

962
00:35:51,569 --> 00:35:53,267
- What's on your mind?

963
00:35:53,267 --> 00:35:55,649
- Nobody has any guns yet,

964
00:35:55,649 --> 00:35:57,778
if it weren't for me,
you'd be rotting in jail.

965
00:35:57,778 --> 00:36:00,255
I wanna make sure I get that 50 grand.

966
00:36:00,255 --> 00:36:01,864
- We keep bargains.

967
00:36:01,864 --> 00:36:03,921
- I just thought I'd tell ya.

968
00:36:03,921 --> 00:36:05,201
- Hi.

969
00:36:05,201 --> 00:36:07,193
- I'm a good shot, and if you try anything

970
00:36:07,193 --> 00:36:08,536
I'll kill all three of you.

971
00:36:08,536 --> 00:36:10,807
- And if you try
something, we'll kill you.

972
00:36:10,807 --> 00:36:12,863
- Well, I guess I had that coming.

973
00:36:12,863 --> 00:36:15,696
- Now that we've bonded, let's go.

974
00:36:17,089 --> 00:36:19,498
- Well, this is gonna be fun.

975
00:36:19,498 --> 00:36:21,915
('80s music)

976
00:36:26,063 --> 00:36:26,896
- Honey?

977
00:36:26,896 --> 00:36:27,737
- Shut up, Iris.

978
00:36:27,737 --> 00:36:29,117
- It's lovely.

979
00:36:29,117 --> 00:36:31,445
- Yeah, it's great, isn't it?

980
00:36:31,445 --> 00:36:32,643
- Just lovely.

981
00:36:32,643 --> 00:36:36,862
- Nah, I'm gonna dredge
it and put up condos.

982
00:36:36,862 --> 00:36:40,300
- Bit cynical, after you
have a few little oil wells,

983
00:36:40,300 --> 00:36:42,099
you wouldn't have to spend any time--

984
00:36:42,099 --> 00:36:43,207
- What's that?

985
00:36:43,207 --> 00:36:45,025
Hold on I have a great
big wax ball up here.

986
00:36:45,025 --> 00:36:46,213
- Will you?

987
00:36:46,213 --> 00:36:48,019
- No, I guess not.

988
00:36:48,019 --> 00:36:49,686
- Nice little scene.

989
00:36:50,879 --> 00:36:53,040
- Oh, the two plots are
in a collision course.

990
00:36:53,040 --> 00:36:55,230
- Really a good time to spring and leave.

991
00:36:55,230 --> 00:36:58,407
- If I ever see that lousy
Louie again I'll break his neck.

992
00:36:58,407 --> 00:37:00,186
- Josie, what do we do now?

993
00:37:00,186 --> 00:37:01,827
- Hitch a ride, I guess.

994
00:37:01,827 --> 00:37:03,577
- Hey, wait a minute.

995
00:37:04,456 --> 00:37:05,840
- We don't have to do anything!

996
00:37:05,840 --> 00:37:07,923
Here comes Touch Conners.

997
00:37:09,052 --> 00:37:11,279
- Hey, look over there!

998
00:37:11,279 --> 00:37:13,946
- Some girls, in primary colors.

999
00:37:16,143 --> 00:37:17,452
- Come on, over here.

1000
00:37:17,452 --> 00:37:19,473
- Stupid, son of a, get over here!

1001
00:37:19,473 --> 00:37:21,185
We just wanna kill you for a minute.

1002
00:37:21,185 --> 00:37:23,018
Yeah, closer, come on.

1003
00:37:25,880 --> 00:37:27,213
- Cut it I said!

1004
00:37:28,409 --> 00:37:29,720
- What's your problem, girls?

1005
00:37:29,720 --> 00:37:31,857
- Bob, honey, I'm frightened,
what do they want?

1006
00:37:31,857 --> 00:37:33,735
- Just the boat, pull into shore.

1007
00:37:33,735 --> 00:37:35,982
- Now, wait a minute,
what do you think this is?

1008
00:37:35,982 --> 00:37:37,327
- Uncle Charlie, no!

1009
00:37:37,327 --> 00:37:38,160
(gunshot)

1010
00:37:38,160 --> 00:37:39,993
- Steve, Champ, Ernie.

1011
00:37:45,393 --> 00:37:46,226
- What's the matter with you?

1012
00:37:46,226 --> 00:37:47,559
- Are you crazy?

1013
00:37:49,390 --> 00:37:50,961
- Tudum, tudum yourself!

1014
00:37:50,961 --> 00:37:53,378
You're no match to me mister.

1015
00:37:54,415 --> 00:37:57,790
- I'm binding, can't you tell I'm binding?

1016
00:37:57,790 --> 00:38:01,247
- Oh man, he landed
right on the wax worms.

1017
00:38:01,247 --> 00:38:04,345
- Uh, sorry about Mr. Demeraz.

1018
00:38:04,345 --> 00:38:06,869
- You were in prison, do you know Bubba?

1019
00:38:06,869 --> 00:38:07,702
- What's this?

1020
00:38:07,702 --> 00:38:09,530
Touch Conners is being
helped from the field,

1021
00:38:09,530 --> 00:38:11,841
but he should return in the second half.

1022
00:38:11,841 --> 00:38:14,341
- Splashing water all over me!

1023
00:38:19,174 --> 00:38:20,591
- Ow, ow, ow, ow.

1024
00:38:25,266 --> 00:38:26,933
- What's your dream?

1025
00:38:30,061 --> 00:38:32,023
- What's the matter?

1026
00:38:32,023 --> 00:38:33,440
- Oh, my fantasy!

1027
00:38:34,985 --> 00:38:36,555
- Oh, she can't take it there.

1028
00:38:36,555 --> 00:38:38,555
She can't take it there.

1029
00:38:41,750 --> 00:38:43,331
- Come on, break it up.

1030
00:38:43,331 --> 00:38:44,907
- We've got guests.

1031
00:38:44,907 --> 00:38:47,000
- What's the matter?

1032
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:49,229
- That guy was going to hit
you in the head with an oar

1033
00:38:49,229 --> 00:38:51,155
and I shot him and she jumped me.

1034
00:38:51,155 --> 00:38:52,727
- I'll hold it.

1035
00:38:52,727 --> 00:38:54,749
- You both came to see
me, that's a first step.

1036
00:38:54,749 --> 00:38:55,852
- There shouldn't be any shooting.

1037
00:38:55,852 --> 00:38:57,018
- What's the matter, you chicken?

1038
00:38:57,018 --> 00:38:57,990
- In case you wanna know,

1039
00:38:57,990 --> 00:38:59,936
shots make noise, and noise carries.

1040
00:38:59,936 --> 00:39:01,583
There's no reason why we should attract

1041
00:39:01,583 --> 00:39:03,407
anymore attention than we have to.

1042
00:39:03,407 --> 00:39:04,391
- Says who?

1043
00:39:04,391 --> 00:39:05,726
- She's gotta point.

1044
00:39:05,726 --> 00:39:07,148
Now quit the fighting.

1045
00:39:07,148 --> 00:39:08,121
Give her back her gun.

1046
00:39:08,121 --> 00:39:09,160
- Who wants guns?

1047
00:39:09,160 --> 00:39:10,731
- [Bots] I do, I do!

1048
